<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblPageDescription">Tell us about your current lobbying activity. Complete all that apply. You must choose at least one option:</span></p>

<p><img id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_imgHelpLegislativeProposal" class="ux-img-valign " src="../../../Stylesheets/Images/help_0.gif">
<span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblLegislativeProposal">Legislative proposal</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblLegislativeProposalAnswer">No</span></b></p>


<p><img id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_imgHelpBill" class="ux-img-valign " src="../../../Stylesheets/Images/help_0.gif">
<span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblBill">Bill or resolution</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblBillAnswer">No</span></b></p>


<p><img id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_imgHelpRegulation" class="ux-img-valign " src="../../../Stylesheets/Images/help_0.gif">
<span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblRegulation">Regulation</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblRegulationAnswer">Yes</span></b></p>

<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucRegulation_lblGoalDescription">Describe your lobbying goal(s) in detail.  What are you attempting to influence or accomplish as a result of your communications with Ontario public office holders?</span></p>
<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucRegulation_txtGoalDescription">- Ontario Environmental Protection Act (EPA); Environmental Approvals under the Ontario EPA. 
Outcome:  Ensure that vehicle manufacturers receive timely approvals and flexibility for their operations to avoid any disruptions and ensure efficient compliance with Ontario EPA approvals.

- O. Reg. 419/05: Air Pollution – Local Air Quality.  
Outcome: Ensure that the point of impingement standards established are achievable and practical for the motor manufacturing to meet requirements 

- Ontario Labour Relations Act and Ontario Employment Standards Act
Outcome: Ensure that changes to the Ontario LRA and Ontario ESA support the competitiveness of plants in Ontario.

Bill 151 - Resource Recovery and Circular Economy Act. Outcome: Ensure implementation does not add undue complexity or regulatory burden for regulations transitioning to the individual producer responsibility approach. 

Bill 4 - Cap &amp; Trade Cancellation Act. Outcome: Ensure that the climate change plan carbon pricing policy does not compromise but protects the auto industry's competitiveness as it is at a significant risk of carbon leakage and highly trade exposed.</span></p>
